<meta type=article>
  <title | Config unknown-kwargs fixture>
  <author | Test Author>
</meta>

<config title="Title in the wrong place" foo-bar="some-value">

<section | Introduction>

This document deliberately abuses `<config>` to trigger the unknown-kwarg
warnings (formerly AUD-13). `title=` is a metadata-shaped kwarg and should
trigger the "did you mean `<meta>`?" hint. `foo-bar=` is an unknown kwarg
and should trigger the generic unknown-kwarg warning. Both kwargs must be
dropped from the config map — they were silently absorbed before the fix
and would have shown up nowhere in the rendered output.
